<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 8 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">China, Dynasty by Dynasty</h1><p class="path-tagline">Two thousand years of the world's most durable state tradition.</p><p class="path-intro">No polity on earth has been reinvented as many times as China. This path takes the dynastic story in sequence - Han foundations, Tang cosmopolitanism and its great rebellion, Song brilliance, the Mongol century, Ming voyages and walls, and the Qing empire at its vast height - asking each time what survived the fall and carried over.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Timekeeper</a> · <a href="/start">the Builder</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/han-dynasty"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liu-bang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Profile · 206 BCE – 220 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Han Dynasty</span><span class="path-step-why">The dynasty that defined China: the examination ideal, the historian's craft and the Silk Road.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/tang-dynasty"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Profile · 618 CE – 907 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Tang Dynasty</span><span class="path-step-why">Chang'an at its height was the largest, most cosmopolitan city on earth.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Event · 755–763</span><span class="path-step-name">An Lushan Rebellion</span><span class="path-step-why">The catastrophe of 755 that broke the Tang world and echoed for a century.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/song-dynasty"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bi-sheng.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Profile · 960 CE – 1279 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Song Dynasty</span><span class="path-step-why">Paper money, printing, gunpowder and the richest economy of the medieval world.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/yuan-dynasty"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kublai-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Profile · 1271 CE – 1368 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Yuan Dynasty</span><span class="path-step-why">The Mongol century: China inside the largest land empire in history.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/ming-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Profile · 1368 CE – 1644 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Ming Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">Restoration, the Forbidden City, and the choice to turn inward.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-he"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zheng-he.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Encyclopedia · Person</span><span class="path-step-name">Zheng He</span><span class="path-step-why">The admiral whose treasure fleets reached Africa decades before the Portuguese.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/qing-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/opium-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">8 · Profile · 1644 CE – 1912 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Qing Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">The last dynasty doubled China's size, then met the nineteenth century.</span></span></a></li></ol>
